      "reasons": [
        "The definition states that evaluation is “the systematic study of whether change has occurred and how it develops over time,” but the provided packet does not explicitly define evaluation in those terms (it mainly critiques reliance on pre–post difference scores and argues for an ontological shift in methods).",
        "The definition claims that evaluation is “most valid” when it examines “change as an unfolding, phase-structured process” rather than only comparing before-and-after scores; while the packet argues change should be treated as continuous, phase-structured (and contrasts this with pre–post difference scores), it does not literally frame this as “most valid” in the sense of establishing normative validity language."
